<title>USA: Neiman Marcus Oct same-store sales up.</title>
<headline>Neiman Marcus Oct same-store sales up.</headline>
<dateline>CHESTNUT HILL, Mass. 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>November 2, 1996    October 28, 1995  % Chg</p>
<p> Total Revenues  $182.4 million     $166.1 million    +9.8%</p>
<p>Comparable</p>
<p>  Revenues	 $175.9 million     $166.1 million    +5.9%</p>
<p>				    13 weeks ended</p>
<p>		    November 2, 1996    October 28,1995   % Chg</p>
<p> Total Revenues  $544.4 million     $490.0 million   +11.1%</p>
<p>Comparable</p>
<p>  Revenues	 $523.5 million     $490.0 million    +6.8%</p>
<p>(a)  Fiscal year ends August 2, 1997.</p>
<p>The Neiman Marcus Group consists of three operating units: Neiman Marcus Stores, NM Direct and Bergdorf Goodman. Harcourt General, Inc. owns approximately 65% of the fully diluted common equity in The Neiman Marcus Group.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
